    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1341ae04-24b4-578f-8f96-335325ca7ed2",
      ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5p+6q &=1 \\\\ 2p+q &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that the system is already organized so that the variables are in the order $p,q$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient.\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-5 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0e070f70-81b6-5313-af6a-ab148a05db8d",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
